},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The announced period begins 4 January 2026 and lasts “until further notice”; the amendment is to be gazetted later, so the relationship between announcement date, commencement date and gazettal is unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0","d802c45a4262c.u6.1357"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Applicability depends on instrument classification, absence of central clearing, licensed-corporation status, the Part III Schedule 10 requirement, and whether the circular operates before gazettal. EU and UK materials explain alignment but do not themselves determine SFC scope.","source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0","d802c45a4262c.u1.381","d802c45a4262c.u3.801","d802c45a4262c.u4.1019","d802c45a4262c.u6.1357","d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"questions":["Does the announced exemption have operative effect from 4 January 2026 before the Part III Schedule 10 amendment is gazetted?","Does “licensed corporations” cover all transactions of a licensed corporation, including offshore booking or counterparties outside the SFC perimeter?","Are any EU-style monitoring or reporting conditions intended to apply in Hong Kong, or are they explanatory background only?","What precise contractual or product features determine that an option is a single-stock, equity-basket or equity-index option and is non-centrally cleared?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The selected control concerns whether an SFC licensed corporation may treat a specified option exposure as exempt from the SFC margin requirement on a stated date.","The option is classified as one of the three listed types and is not centrally cleared.","No EU or UK condition is imported unless the SFC text expressly adopts it."],"citations":[{"quote":"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"},{"quote":"As set out in Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"}],"distinction":"Reading A treats the circular as an operative announcement: from 2026-01-04, the listed non-centrally cleared equity options are exempt for licensed corporations, despite the later gazettal statement. The foreign EU and UK provisions are alignment context only.","family":"modality","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is a corporation licensed by or registered with the SFC under the Code of Conduct context.","name":"licensed_corporation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0","d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"],"type":"bool","unit":"boolean"},{"meaning":"The transaction is a non-centrally cleared single-stock, equity-basket or equity-index option.","name":"qualifying_non_cleared_equity_option","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessment date is on or after 2026-01-04.","name":"assessment_on_or_after_2026_01_04","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"boolean"},{"meaning":"The announced exemption remains in force because no further notice ending it has been identified.","name":"exemption_until_further_notice","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"boolean"}],"result":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] The selected exemption condition is satisfied when the actor is a licensed corporation, the option qualifies, the assessment date is on or after 2026-01-04, and the exemption remains in force. False means at least one of those conditions is not established; it does not determine whether the underlying Code amendment has been gazetted.","result_type":"bool","scope":"A selected SFC margin-exemption control for one licensed corporation and one option exposure."},"local_id":"reading_a","questions":["Whether the circular alone is legally sufficient before gazettal remains unresolved."],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Under the announced-operational reading, the selected SFC exemption condition is satisfied for a licensed corporation's qualifying non-centrally cleared equity option assessed on or after 2026-01-04 while the exemption remains in force.","subject":"SFC margin-exemption applicability"},{"assumptions":["The Code amendment and gazettal are prerequisites for operative legal exemption.","The announcement signals intended future alignment but does not itself disapply the existing Part III requirement before gazettal."],"citations":[{"quote":"Paragraph 7(e) of Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357"},{"quote":"The margin requirements for non-centrally cleared equity options were originally scheduled to take effect on that date.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u1.381"},{"quote":"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"}],"distinction":"Reading B treats the circular as a prospective policy announcement whose operative effect depends on the promised Code amendment and gazettal. Before that event, the existing margin requirement remains applicable; after gazettal, the listed options are exempt from 2026-01-04 or the gazettal commencement date, whichever the amendment specifies.","family":"time","formalization":null,"local_id":"reading_b","questions":["The text does not state whether gazettal is constitutive, merely formal, or retroactive to 2026-01-04.","The text does not specify the commencement date in the eventual amendment."],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Under the gazettal-dependent reading, the exemption condition is satisfied only once the required Code amendment has been gazetted and its commencement requirements are met; the circular alone does not establish that condition before then.","subject":"SFC margin-exemption applicability"}]},"run_id":"run.4fdb750c6efe483289f180eee6e68ed2"}